Data sources read at runtime
----------------------------

Crosswalk reads these sources only through Zetaris. No bulk data from them
is distributed in this repository.

OpenFEMA (Federal Emergency Management Agency)
  DisasterDeclarationsSummaries (v2) and OpenFemaDataSets (v1) at
  www.fema.gov/api/open. Public US federal data, no key. FEMA is cited as
  the source; this project is not endorsed by FEMA.

SEC EDGAR (U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission)
  XBRL frames and submissions APIs at data.sec.gov. A work of the U.S.
  government. Read live under the SEC fair-access policy (at most 10
  requests per second, with a declared User-Agent), never redistributed.
  The repository commits no extracted SEC values: the documentation cites
  revenue only as year-on-year percentage changes. seeds/utilities.json
  holds public identifiers only (CIK, name, ticker, SIC, headquarters
  state) with the curated states served and station ids.

NOAA GHCN-Daily (National Centers for Environmental Information)
  Parquet files and ghcnd-stations.txt on the Registry of Open Data on AWS,
  bucket noaa-ghcn-pds. CC0 1.0 (a work of the U.S. government). Cite:
  Menne, M.J., I. Durre, B. Korzeniewski, S. McNeill, K. Thomas, X. Yin,
  S. Anthony, R. Ray, R.S. Vose, B.E. Gleason, and T.G. Houston, 2012:
  Global Historical Climatology Network - Daily (GHCN-Daily), Version 3.
  NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information. seeds/stations.json
  holds station ids, names and states from ghcnd-stations.txt.

company_dns
  SIC code list served at company-dns.mediumroast.io (V4). The service is
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; the SIC codes and
  descriptions are the SEC's. Called with an identifying User-Agent.

Zetaris getting-started repository (optional, at boot)
  https://github.com/zetaris/getting-started, Apache License, Version 2.0.
  When ZETARIS_GETTING_STARTED_DIR is set, its open_data/manifest.json and
  known_to_fail notes are read to seed the catalogue and H-MEM. Nothing
  from it is redistributed here.


Models and platforms (not redistributed)
----------------------------------------

NVIDIA Nemotron (nemotron-3-nano:4b) runs locally through Ollama under the
NVIDIA Open Model License. The model weights are not redistributed in this
repository.

Zetaris Lightning 2.4.3.1 and its JDBC driver are installed from Zetaris
under Zetaris's terms. Neither is redistributed in this repository.
